    "created_at": "2022-03-04T23:05:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-04T23:05:32Z",
    "body": "Allowed to navigate is almost entirely about sandboxing. Maybe it was about something else at the time this issue was raised?\r\n\r\nYou can have pages which same-origin and sandbox using allow-same-origin, while not allowed to navigate each other (because they don't have allow-top-navigation or similar). So this flag is not obsolete; it's necessary for such cases.",
